--- WEB SOURCE PARITY (the spec) ---
ConflictWarnings({ conflicts }) is a pure presentational list (only hook: useTranslation):
  * conflicts.length === 0  -> returns null
  * else conflicts.map -> <AlertBanner variant title icon>"name": reason</AlertBanner>
      variant = severity === 'warning' ? 'warning' : 'info'
      icon    = severity === 'warning' ? <AlertTriangle/> : <Info/>
      title   = t('automations.builder.conflict','Potential Conflict')   (the ONLY i18n key in source)
      body    = `"${automation_name}": ${reason}`               (no onClose -> non-dismissible)
Native reproduction:
  * AlertBanner          -> TsAlertBanner (Components.Feedback), Dismissible=false (no web onClose)
  * AlertTriangle / Info -> Segoe Fluent glyphs E7BA / E946 (the TsBanner variant defaults)
  * states: Loading (skeleton) / Empty (TsEmptyState, native replacement for web `return null`) / Ready (space-y-2 stack)
    error/stale/offline are NOT in the web source: it never fetches; the hosting AutomationBuilderPage owns the
    conflict-check lifecycle (same rationale as the WindowStatusDetail / HighlightCard presentational ports).
  * i18n keys (ALL present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw):
      translation.automations.builder.conflict  ("Potential Conflict")
      translation.common.noData                 ("No data available", empty surface)
      translation.common.loading                ("Loading", loading surface)
  * Telemetry: view.opened slug=ConflictWarnings (P1/S11), PII-safe (never logs automation name/reason/id).

